# Daily CRM - environment template
#
# THIS APP RUNS ON VERCEL. These variables belong in
# Vercel > Project > Settings > Environment Variables, ticked for Production.
#
# They are read at BUILD time, so adding one to an existing deployment does
# nothing until you redeploy with the build cache off. That is the step that
# catches people.
#
# This file is committed as the checklist of what is needed - it never holds a
# real value. (For local development, copy it to .env.local, which is
# gitignored.)
#
# Values come from Supabase > Project Settings > API.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required. Safe to expose to a browser - Row Level Security is what protects
# the data, so a rep holding this key can still only read their own players.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional, server only. Needed for exactly two things: creating a login from
# the People page, and blocking sign-in when someone is deactivated. Everything
# else in the app works without it.
#
# This key bypasses Row Level Security completely. Never prefix it with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never commit it.
#
# Without it, Admin > People cannot create or block logins, and says so.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Wager leaderboards are NOT configured here. There can be several, each with
# its own key, so they are managed in the app: Admin > Settings > Wager
# sources. Keys are stored in an admin-only table and shown masked after
# saving.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional, server only. Enables the hourly automatic wager sync.
#
# Any long random string - generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
#
# Without it the /api/cron/wager-sync endpoint refuses to run, which is
# deliberate: an unauthenticated sync URL would let anyone on the internet
# hammer the Roobet API using your keys.
#
# The schedule itself lives in vercel.json and starts working once deployed.
# Vercel sends this value automatically as a Bearer token; any external
# scheduler can do the same.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CRON_SECRET=
